According to Google Pay Help , both Google and Plaid store account details and transaction history while an account is linked. Using Wallet with Gemini also requires Keep Activity to be on, so chats are saved to Gemini Apps Activity. Google says human reviewers review a subset of Connected Apps data, including inferences from Google Wallet and payment services information. Disconnecting Wallet does not, by itself, remove account information from past chats. The connection is for adults in the United States using a personal Google Account. If you want transaction data kept out of an artificial intelligence (AI) product, use a manual budget instead. The published pages considered here do not answer how long Gemini keeps chat content containing account details or how Plaid treats data after you unlink an account inside Google Wallet. Tools for this journey Monthly Budget Calculator → Should You Connect Your Bank Accounts to Gemini? Connect your bank accounts to Gemini through Google Wallet if you want to ask questions about spending and accept the account-data and chat-activity trade-offs. Google says Gemini can use transactions from linked accounts to review expenses and suggest budgets. Google also says its access is read-only: Gemini cannot move, manage or invest your money. You can start with Google Wallet information without linking a bank account through Plaid. The Gemini Apps Help page describes Wallet questions about available rewards, special offers, boarding passes and airline loyalty numbers. Linking a financial account through Plaid adds transaction and balance information for spending questions. Decide whether those added answers are worth sharing your account information before linking. Do not connect if you want transaction history kept out of Gemini. A manual budget lets you work from amounts you enter yourself. The connection is also unavailable to people using work, school or supervised Google Accounts, and to people under 18 or outside the United States. Google says the Wallet feature requires Keep Activity to be on. If saved Gemini chats are unacceptable to you, that requirement settles the decision. Google lets you turn the Wallet connection off later. Removing information already used in a chat takes another action: you must delete the chats containing it. Unlinking a financial account inside Wallet is separate again. Those are distinct decisions about Gemini access, chat history and the bank link, so consider all three before opting in. What Gemini Can See Through Google Wallet and Plaid Gemini can use Google Wallet information and transaction data from financial accounts you link through services such as Plaid. Google's Connected Apps Help page lists payment methods, receipts, data from Google services saved in Wallet and linked financial account information. The Wallet-specific Help page says Gemini can summarize expenses, offer budgeting tips, and check rewards or special offers associated with cards and passes. Google's examples show the kinds of questions the connection is meant to answer. You can ask how much you spent on groceries last month. You can ask about subscriptions across linked accounts and whether recurring charges rose in price this year. Another example asks Gemini to review last year's gifts and travel transactions and suggest a holiday budget. Google's launch post also describes a spending review aimed at saving $1,000 over the next three months. It says Gemini can generate charts for cash flow, asset allocation and budgets in the chat. Those are examples of prompts and described responses, not a promise that a suggested budget will save $1,000. Google says you connect Wallet under Connected Apps in Gemini's Personal Intelligence settings. You can then tag @Google Wallet in a prompt. If Gemini does not use Wallet when you expect it to, Google's Help page says to mention Google Wallet or add @Google Wallet to the question. A bank link is not the only type of financial link described in the launch material. Plaid's announcement says people can link bank accounts, credit cards, loans and investment accounts to Google Wallet through Plaid. The useful question before linking any of them is whether you want Gemini to draw on the resulting financial information for answers in chat. What Gemini Cannot Do With Your Money Google says the Google Wallet connection gives Gemini read-only access to linked accounts, so Gemini cannot move, manage or invest your money. Google's Help page also says Gemini cannot make transactions with Wallet payment methods or update or delete connected financial accounts. You make account changes in Google Wallet settings. Capability What Gemini does or cannot do Source Read transactions from linked accounts Can use transaction data to provide spending insights Gemini Apps Help Summarize spending and budgets Can summarize expenses and give budgeting tips Gemini Apps Help Summarize rewards and offers Can check available rewards and special offers based on Wallet cards and passes Gemini Apps Help Move or invest money Cannot move, manage or invest money, according to Google Google's launch post Make transactions with Wallet payment methods Cannot make transactions using those payment methods Gemini Apps Help Update or delete linked accounts Cannot do either. Account changes happen in Google Wallet settings Gemini Apps Help These are Google's descriptions of the connected app's capabilities. Read-only access limits actions Gemini can take with your money. It does not tell you what Google or Plaid store, and it does not establish how long chat content containing account information remains in Gemini. Judge the connection's privacy cost separately from its inability to make a payment. What Google and Plaid Store While Your Accounts Are Linked Google Pay Help says both Google and Plaid store financial and identity information while an account is linked through Plaid. Its list includes a credit card or bank account number, a bank routing number when applicable, transaction history, account balance, name, address, phone number and email address. Google says Plaid collects and uses your financial institution login information to access your account and obtain transaction and balance information. Plaid says it does not share your financial institution username and password with apps. Plaid also says it transfers data through its application programming interface (API) and uses Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) 256-bit and Transport Layer Security (TLS) encryption. Those statements describe Plaid's handling of a connection. They do not remove the account numbers, balances, transactions and identity details that Google's Help page says both organizations store while an account is linked. The Gemini setting adds a separate record to consider. Google's Wallet Help page says Keep Activity must be on to connect Google Wallet. While Keep Activity is on, Gemini chats are saved in Gemini Apps Activity. A spending question can therefore become part of a saved chat as well as an answer drawn from linked information. You can review what you plan to link before turning on the Gemini connection. If you need a grocery total, consider whether sharing the listed account and identity information is an acceptable way to get it. Who Can Use It Today Google says Google Wallet in Gemini is available to eligible adults in the United States using a personal Google Account. You must be at least 18, use English and have Keep Activity on. The feature works in the Gemini mobile app and the Gemini web app at gemini.google.com. Google's Help page says it is unavailable with work, school or supervised Google Accounts, and does not work in certain Gemini features, including Gems and Gemini Live. Google's November 13, 2026, launch post describes a rollout to all Gemini app users in the United States across the web and mobile apps on Android and iOS. Its Help page says Google is making the feature available gradually, so an eligible person may not see it yet. If Connected Apps does not show Google Wallet, gradual availability is one possibility. Keep Activity being off or signing in with an ineligible account would also prevent the connection under Google's stated requirements. Availability is separate from whether a particular bank link remains connected. Google Pay Help says a bank can interrupt a link for security maintenance, credentials can change, a linked card can expire, or an account may no longer be found. It also lists unsupported multi-factor authentication (MFA) as a possible cause. For an account that was linked and then disconnected, Google directs you to Settings, Accounts linked with Plaid, then Reconnect. Google says transactions can take several minutes to appear after linking or reconnecting. How to Turn Off Google Wallet in Gemini and Delete Your Data Removing linked financial information from Gemini requires you to address both the Wallet connection and chats containing that information. Google's Gemini Help page says disconnecting the app alone can leave information in a past chat. Deleting chats alone can leave Gemini able to find information through the connected app. Unlinking the underlying account in Google Wallet is a further, separate step. Disconnect Google Wallet in Gemini. In the mobile app, open Menu, tap your profile picture or initial, then choose Personal Intelligence and Connected Apps. Turn Google Wallet off. On the Gemini web app, open Menu, Settings, Personal Intelligence and Connected Apps, then use More options and Disconnect. Delete chats containing the information. Use Gemini Apps Activity or Recent chats to delete all chats that contain the account information you want removed. Google says you must both delete those chats and disconnect the app. If you skip either action, Gemini might still use information from the remaining chat or connected app. Unlink financial accounts if you also want to end the bank connection. On the Google Wallet website, choose Settings, then Accounts linked with Plaid. Select an account, click Unlink and confirm. Google Pay Help says Google deletes the transaction history associated with an account when you remove that account from Google Wallet. Manage data held by Plaid separately. Plaid says its Portal lets you disconnect accounts from apps or delete your data from Plaid's systems. Google Pay Help says Plaid continues to store data for accounts linked through Plaid with a non-Google service. Manage those connections through Plaid. The pages considered here do not say how Plaid treats data after you unlink an account inside Google Wallet, so do not treat a Wallet unlink as a stated Plaid deletion step. Google's launch post also says you can open Profile, Personal Intelligence and Memory Summary to view, refine or remove details Gemini saved about your preferences, interests and goals. Memory Summary controls are distinct from deleting chats containing financial information. Turning Personal Intelligence off for one chat does not stop that chat from being saved to Gemini Apps Activity or used to personalize another response. Google says to use a temporary chat if you want to chat without saving activity to your Google Account. Privacy Trade-Offs for Budgeting The privacy trade-off is whether conversational answers about spending are worth linking financial information to Google Wallet and Gemini. Google's examples include reviewing last quarter's spending, finding recurring subscriptions and using last year's gifts and travel spending to suggest a holiday budget. A question about rewards or a boarding pass may use Wallet information without the additional step of linking a financial account through Plaid. For questions about transactions across linked accounts, the Plaid link supplies the account information Gemini uses. In our reading of Google's Help pages, read-only access settles one concern: Gemini cannot use the connected app to move money or make a Wallet payment. Google Pay Help says Google and Plaid store account details, balances, transaction history and basic identity information while accounts are linked. Google's Gemini Help page requires Keep Activity on for the connection, which means chats are saved in Gemini Apps Activity. Three further points come from the published material used for this decision: The pages do not answer how long Gemini keeps chat content that contains account details. They do not answer how Plaid treats your data after you unlink an account inside Google Wallet. Google's statement that it deletes that account's transaction history is a statement about Google's handling, not Plaid's. Google's Connected Apps data page says human reviewers review a subset of data processed by Gemini, including summaries, excerpts and inferences from Google Wallet and payment services information. It also says Gemini Apps activity can be used to improve Google services, including training generative AI models, when Keep Activity is on. If those gaps affect your choice, leave the bank link off. You can enter figures yourself in the monthly budget calculator rather than connecting an account to Gemini. If you want to compare other approaches to tracking spending, the best budgeting apps list covers alternatives. Decide how much account access you are willing to grant before choosing one. For an adult in the United States using a personal Google Account, connecting makes sense only if the spending questions are useful enough to justify the listed storage and saved chats. Skip the connection if you want transactions kept out of an AI product. Work, school and supervised accounts are ineligible. A published answer on Gemini chat retention or Plaid's handling after a Wallet unlink could change the privacy assessment. So could a change to Google's stated read-only access or data-use terms. Check Google Wallet in Gemini's requirements on Google's Wallet Help page before you opt in. Frequently asked questions Is Google Wallet in Gemini safe? Google says Gemini's access is read-only, so it cannot move, manage or invest money through the connection. That is not a safety guarantee. Google Pay Help says Google and Plaid store account details and transaction history while an account is linked. Google says human reviewers review a subset of Connected Apps data, including Wallet inferences. The pages considered here do not say how long Gemini keeps chat content containing account details. Is Google Wallet in Gemini free? The Google pages considered here do not state a price for the Wallet connection. Plaid says it does not charge you to connect accounts and that the app pays Plaid a fee. Its consumer page names Venmo and Oportun as examples, not Google Wallet. That does not establish a price for every account or service you might use. How do I turn off Google Wallet in Gemini? Turn off Google Wallet under Personal Intelligence and Connected Apps in Gemini. To remove information Gemini may still use from past conversations, also delete every chat containing it from Gemini Apps Activity or Recent chats. Google says both actions are needed. If you also want to remove a linked financial account, unlink it separately under Accounts linked with Plaid in Google Wallet settings. Can Gemini move money or pay bills from Google Wallet? No. Google says the connected app gives Gemini read-only access and cannot move, manage or invest money. Google's Help page also says Gemini cannot make transactions using Wallet payment methods. Does Google Wallet in Gemini work with a work account? No. Google says the connection requires a personal Google Account and is unavailable for work, school and supervised accounts. You must also be at least 18, be in the United States, use English and have Keep Activity on. Why is Google Wallet in Gemini not working for me? Google says the feature is becoming available gradually, even though its launch post describes a rollout across the United States. Check the eligibility requirements on 